+# Reference Name snapshot endpoint cardinality
+
+SOURCE ONLY; all new syntax, portable/PS tests and qualification execution UNRUN. Direct parent is the frozen test-owned native-temp leaf781028f73be79341b9bac6fab078e8416ddd8539. No Office assignment or existing failure is changed.
+
+Preserve actual Windows validation43160756096/job130991095157: Node9tests8PASS/1FAIL, PS1.92s, first private adapter positive refused completion before observer IO. The native-temp correction worked (`lexicalSpellingDiffers=true`, `sameOwnedFixture=true`), but the original32 managed controls remain unqualified. Exact43-file evidence is retained at `/tmp/opf-name-snapshot-temp-validation-review01/payload`; ZIP138163B SHA256 `9d3ee465b9120ccfb9cdb0bc0e406d9f118b5424519b09296a83ab5937b1ac2d`.
+
+The actual readiness function assigns `$end=if(...)` then checks `$end.Count`. Statement output unwraps the one selected JSON PSCustomObject. Windows PowerShell5.1 has no Count property for that object, so the exact-one predicate refuses. Retained actual rows have no Count member: before35→setter53 and reopened104→close106; both endpoints have exactly one row and valid owners/order/status. Microsoft [about_PSCustomObject Notes](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/microsoft.powershell.core/about/about_pscustomobject#notes) documents this version difference. This is a source and retained-record diagnosis; no new actual first-false trace or PS execution is claimed.
+
+Wrap only the complete conditional in `@(...)`. Both success filters, Count1 predicate, order comparison and every other readiness/observer guard remain exact. Add a separately named cardinality result group containing six actual-function controls: zero/one/two success endpoints for each of the before/reopened branches. The whole unchanged function must return true for singleton positives and false for zero/duplicates; no mocked subguard or rewritten function is used. Original8startup+13Save+11adapter scenarios remain their separate32 group, and the full private adapter positive still exercises the complete real readiness-to-observer chain. The same nine Node groups now also require the exact six names, row counts and boolean outcomes. Original15-second PS child deadline, source/archive/mode/ownership/kernel/observer bounds and TEMP/TMP/cwd behavior remain unchanged. Actual PS execution is still owed; six new controls are not a retroactive38-pass claim.
